From 777ed07fc4e97ad6ac00bceb54d9146c700cdc95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:45:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): a jstack task reads stalled only where jbus says
 its crew owes the next move

A crew is idle by design once its pull request is up, so the tree said stalled of nearly every
pull request older than the quiet threshold, also of one that CI, its reviewer, jmerge or
another row holds. jbus already judges who holds each row's next move (work.json's who), so
the task carries it from work.json to the tree, and idleOf says stalled only where who is crew.
The row's tooltip and the head of its menu say what jbus says it waits on, such as waits on the
check runner.
